<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH 1,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH 1,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Irish 1,000 Guineas</p>
<p>for three-year-old fillies run over one mile (1.6 km) at The</p>
<p>Curragh on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Classic Park	 20-1	(ridden by Stephen Craine)</p>
<p> 2. Strawberry Roan     4-1	(Christy Roche)</p>
<p> 3. Caiseal Ros	  20-1	(Kevin Manning)</p>
<p>10 ran. Ryafan was the 3-1 favourite</p>
<p>Distances: One length, two-and-a-half-lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Mrs Seamus Burns and trained in Ireland by</p>
<p>Aidan O'Brien.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 84,250 pounds ($126,375).</p>
